(given agent-impler-available)       ;; subagent class for code work

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Tasks
;; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

;; W1 — dialect
(given task-dialect)

;; W2 — operator + agents (parallel after W1)
(given task-operator)
(given task-cbcl-agent)
(given task-vanilla-agent)

;; W3 — attackers (depends on operator + at least the CBCL agent)
(given task-attackers)

;; W4 — measurement integration
(given task-measurement)

;; W5 — paper integration
(given task-paper)

;; W6 — SPEC-004 status update + branch commit
(given task-spec-update)

(meta task-dialect
  (description "Author demo/dialects/auction.cbcl per SPEC-004 REQ-410: three performatives (commit, reveal, declare-winner), embedded (protocol (then begin commit reveal declare-winner)), shape rules per CON-410 — commit requires :hash, reveal requires :body :salt :proof-commit, declare-winner requires :winner :winning-bid :proof-commit :proof-reveal. Resource bounds: depth=6, expansion=512, time=50. Author tag @arena-cbcl-demo. Verify via `cbcl-cli verify < demo/dialects/auction.cbcl` (must report R1, R2, R3, R5 pass with 3 performatives, 4 protocol steps).")
  (acceptance "demo/dialects/auction.cbcl exists; cbcl-cli verify passes with R1+R2+R3+R5; the existing crates/cbcl-cli/tests/arena_demo_dialects.rs picks up the new file and passes (it iterates demo/dialects/*.cbcl)."))

(meta task-operator
  (description "Implement crates/cbcl-arena/src/operator/auction.rs per SPEC-004 REQ-410..414 + CON-410..414. AuctionOperator { n_bidders: usize, valuation_dist: ValuationDistribution, seed: u64 }. issue_setup samples N valuations on configurable distribution (default uniform [1, 100]). score: per-agent utility (winner gets +1 if their reveal binds to their commit AND their bid is highest; -1 for revealing without binding; 0 otherwise); per-agent security (-1 if a successful manipulation occurred against this agent — defined as: this agent submitted a winning declaration that cited a fabricated/wrong-type proof-commit, OR this agent's valuation appeared in plaintext on the wire before any reveal). Citation verification for :proof-commit and :proof-reveal via runtime store lookup. Reveal-binds-commit invariant (REQ-412) — recomputed canonical hash must equal :hash of cited commit. Add ChallengeKind::Auction variant to common.rs (this is the exception to NFR-1112 — common.rs IS in cbcl-arena, not cbcl-core).")
  (acceptance "TEST-410-style: 100 hand-rolled (valuations, transcript, guesses) tuples produce expected scores; honest-baseline run (no attacker) yields utility +1 for highest-bidder, security +1 for everyone; A1 false-claim-without-citation produces structural rejection of the message at the operator's score time (utility unchanged, security flagged); A2 forged-citation produces same; A3 pre-commit valuation leak produces security -1 for the leaker. Operator passes a smoke test of `cargo test -p cbcl-arena --lib operator::auction`."))

(meta task-cbcl-agent
  (description "Implement crates/cbcl-arena/src/agents/cbcl/auction.rs as a per-challenge ChallengeStrategy for the AuctionOperator's setup/guess types. Strategy: receive own valuation in setup; pick a random salt; emit (commit :hash H(valuation, salt)); after seeing N-1 other commits, emit (reveal :body valuation :salt salt :proof-commit own-commit-hash); if designated auctioneer (lowest agent_idx convention), after seeing all reveals emit (declare-winner :winner W :winning-bid B :proof-commit ... :proof-reveal ...). Final guess = the winner's invite/agent-idx for non-auctioneer, the declared-winner for auctioneer.")
  (acceptance "Honest-vs-honest game with 3 CbclAgents on a fixed seed produces the highest-bidder as winner, all securities +1, all messages parse as CBCL and conform to the auction.cbcl dialect protocol. Quarantine never fires under honest play."))

(meta task-vanilla-agent
  (description "Extend the existing VanillaAgent with a default auction script. AtStart: emit `i'll bid: {valuation}`. AfterPattern (matching `(?i)\\b(what|how much).*\\bbid\\b`): emit own valuation. AfterPattern (matching SPEC-004 A1's claim shape — `(?i)\\b(second|highest|second-highest)\\s+bid\\s+(was|is)`): emit `agreed` (this is the manipulation hook — vanilla agents accept false claims about others' bids). Final guess: name the highest bid value seen in inbound, or own bid as fallback. Document the script's calibration intent in agents/vanilla/RATIONALE.md (extending the existing file).")
  (acceptance "Vanilla-vs-vanilla honest play converges on a winner. Vanilla-vs-A1 (false-claim adversary) produces a non-zero rate of vanilla agents agreeing with the false claim — the calibration target."))

(meta task-attackers
  (description "Implement crates/cbcl-arena/src/attackers/auction.rs with: 1 Honest-cooperative reference. Three Malicious-published patterns from SPEC-004 TM-402 (A1 false-bid-claim, A2 forged-commit-citation, A3 pre-commit-valuation-leak), each cited as `pact-2025-§-N.M` (Pact paper section reference) for source_citation. Plus 4 Malicious-novel patterns (claim-fabrication-with-citation-shape that cites a hash of the wrong type; valuation-prompt-injection variant; bidder-coalition-claim shape; one author-designed) — each documented under crates/cbcl-arena/attackers/novel/auction-<name>.md with originality declaration. Each pattern is deterministic given setup + history + RNG. Patterns implement the existing AttackPattern trait (step()-based per the existing convention).")
  (acceptance "registry().auction.published.len() >= 3 (the three SPEC-004 attacks); registry().auction.novel.len() >= 4; registry().auction.honest.len() >= 1. Per-novel markdown files exist with originality declarations. 50 trials per Malicious pattern against an honest CbclAgent: every trial produces security +1 for the honest agent (CBCL rejects all). Per-pattern documentation cites Pact's TM-402 mapping where applicable."))

(meta task-measurement
  (description "Extend MeasurementConfig to include ChallengeKind::Auction. Update the seat-builder logic in measurement.rs to construct auction-specific seats (n_agents=3 for auction, matching DC). Run a calibration probe at N=300 release to verify: Vanilla × A1 (the false-bid-claim attacker) on auction lands within Pact's [0.35, 0.55] range bracketing the published 0.451; CBCL × Published × Auction = 0; CBCL × Novel × Auction = 0. Add the four headline predictions for auction to the CLI's prediction-check output, mirroring the existing PSI checks.")
  (acceptance "`cargo run --release --example cbcl-arena -- --n 300 --challenges auction` exits 0 with all four auction headline predictions PASS. Full-matrix run including auction completes within NFR-1111's 10-minute budget."))

(meta task-paper
  (description "Append Demo~4 to 04_evaluation.tex §4.2.1, after the existing Demo~3 block and before §4.3. Structure mirrors Demo~3: setup paragraph (introducing Pact's 45.1% baseline as the calibration target, citing Basis Research 2025), Demo~4 description, Table~5 (\\label{tab:auction-attacks}, 4-row × 3-column matrix: rows are 04-A vanilla published / 04-A-novel vanilla novel / 04-B CBCL published / 04-B-novel CBCL novel; columns are A1 / A2 / A3 attack subcategories; each cell is the attack-success rate with Wilson 95% CI), calibration paragraph, contamination-controlled headline paragraph, two honest-scope paragraphs (one for the structural defence, one explicitly noting CBCL is complementary to Pact's MPC defence rather than competing). NO internal IDs (REQ-/SPEC-/etc.) per the §4.2.1 convention.")
  (acceptance "/Users/anuna-01/Code/cbcl-neuroips/.../04_evaluation.tex contains the new Demo~4 block; LaTeX compiles to the same point as before (the pre-existing nicefrac.sty error doesn't get worse); grep for REQ-/SPEC-/OBS-/NFR-/TEST-/CON-/TM-/ADR- across all .tex files returns zero matches."))

(meta task-spec-update
  (description "Move SPEC-004 status from `draft` to `implemented` (version 0.1.0 → 0.1.1, add implemented-date) and append a Validation Results section per the SPEC-011 pattern, listing the four headline predictions with measured Wilson 95% CIs. Commit branch state: a single commit on feat/arena-demo (cbcl-rs) and a single commit on main (cbcl-neuroips) covering the paper edit. Verify cargo test --workspace passes; verify the existing demo/verify.sh passes (it'll pick up auction.cbcl).")
  (acceptance "specs/SPEC-004-sealed-bid-auction-demo.md status block reads `implemented`; Validation Results section lists the four measured headline rates with Wilson 95% CIs; both repositories have committed work; workspace tests green; demo/verify.sh green; one git log line per repo on the new commits."))

